# Pin every text file to LF on every platform's checkout.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows defaults `core.autocrlf=true` and rewrites
# LF -> CRLF on checkout. The repo is authored on Linux/macOS with LF line
# endings, so the CRLF-converted Windows checkout flags every line of every
# file as "wrongly formatted" to Biome, blowing up the verify step and
# burying real Windows-specific test failures under format noise.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect text vs. binary; `eol=lf` then forces
# LF on text files for every checkout, which matches `.editorconfig`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Common binary types — declare them explicitly so Git never tries to
# normalize them, even if `text=auto` misclassifies any of them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
